Z||000000||GT GT 87||11-10-2001||11:31 PM||||I have just assembled the heads onto my 3.2 shortblock. The felpro head gaskets didn't say up or down , and tell you the truth , I can't remember which way I installed them . Is there a up and down ? Or does it matter. This is a new motor , so I had nothing to go by .||||reg||1
Z||000001||samoht||11-10-2001||11:39 PM||||no, but I always put the lettering up...  Dont forget to seal the intake ends real good<P>85gt3.2||||reg||1
Z||000002||StuGood||11-11-2001||12:56 AM||||For the Fel-Pro "Blue Stripe" line of gaskets, a counter guy at Autozone told me the side with blue stripes goes up.  I took his advice (and used it to install a head gasket on a 2.8-l V6 in a Fiero), and it seems to work very well, so far.  <P>Whether it matters which way is up, I don't know.  The counter guy said he "learned over the years" that, for Fel-Pro, it's "blue stripes up."  Didn't know whether he knew anything or not, but decided to give it a try.  The head gasket seems to work very well.<P>It surprises me that they can go to the trouble to print blue stripes all over a gasket, but can't be bothered to print "this side up."  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||GT GT 87||11-11-2001||01:28 AM||||The ones I used were from the Fiero store , Head gasket set , that included everything from the head - up , they didn't have "stripes" ||||reg||1
